Here's one response that we wanted to share from a listener in Newton, Massachusetts. Her name is Deb Pierce. She had a story about an unsung hero who showed up at one of the hardest moments in her life. It's Valentine's Day, 1983, and I've just delivered a baby that lived for an hour and a half. She was born prematurely and I was distraught. And as I lay in my room several hours later, it was the evening and I couldn't fall asleep., I lost a lot of blood and I was, um, had a couple of transfusions. And I felt so alone and I went out to the nurse's unit to see whether anybody might come and sit with me and hold my hand.
这是我们想分享的一位来自马萨诸塞州牛顿市的听众的回应。她叫黛比·皮尔斯。她有一个关于无名英雄的故事，这位英雄出现在她人生中最艰难的时刻之一。那是1983年的情人节，我刚刚生下一个只活了一个半小时的孩子。她是个早产儿，我悲痛欲绝。几个小时后，我躺在病房里，那是傍晚，我睡不着觉。我失血过多，而且，嗯，输了几次血。我感到非常孤独，我走到护士站，看看有没有人能来陪我坐一会儿，握着我的手。

